1
00:00:11,380 --> 00:00:17,540
Aiming for the sunset
floating over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:18,660 --> 00:00:24,660
kick a whetstone and
even your shoes go flying.

3
00:00:24,660 --> 00:00:32,960
Will you have your hair snipped off,
I wonder?

4
00:00:32,960 --> 00:00:39,120
They laughed at me for
still acting like a brat.

5
00:00:39,800 --> 00:00:44,220
Even if you spread some energy somewhere,

6
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:49,280
Katsushika, Kameari,
another yawn, nothing changes.

7
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:53,160
The streets are strangely gentle.

8
00:00:54,660 --> 00:01:01,120
From the pointed-hat water bottle,

9
00:01:01,720 --> 00:01:07,440
the sun sinks toward the vast heavens.

10
00:01:10,740 --> 00:01:15,920
Tomorrow will end just like this too,
won't it.

11
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:21,060
Katsushika, Shibamata,
happiness lost once again.

12
00:01:21,060 --> 00:01:24,480
Because I'm a fool who
only realized it too late.

13
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:31,500
Nakagawa's father,
the ferocious company president

14
00:01:49,700 --> 00:01:51,340
Everyone's gone ahead of us, haven't they?

15
00:01:52,020 --> 00:01:55,260
After all,
everyone's really into their model trains.

16
00:01:55,260 --> 00:01:58,720
That guy spent so much money on model trains

17
00:01:58,720 --> 00:02:00,580
that his wife ran off on him.

18
00:02:01,500 --> 00:02:05,340
And the guy next door, just because
he built a half-scale steam locomotive,

19
00:02:05,390 --> 00:02:08,560
had to buy a new house because he had nowhere to put it.
What an idiot.

20
00:02:08,900 --> 00:02:11,472
But the leader of that bunch of idiots,

21
00:02:11,522 --> 00:02:12,980
that's Ryo-sama, right?

22
00:02:13,420 --> 00:02:15,760
Yes, I'm the biggest fool of them all...

23
00:02:16,540 --> 00:02:18,500
See! Why are you making me say that?!

24
00:02:26,060 --> 00:02:28,020
Steam locomotives really are the best,
aren't they.

25
00:02:28,500 --> 00:02:29,520
Hey, Ryo-san.

26
00:02:31,640 --> 00:02:32,720
Next stop, let's go.

27
00:02:50,180 --> 00:02:52,440
Why are there so many people here?

28
00:02:52,440 --> 00:02:53,740
No wonder, really.

29
00:02:53,740 --> 00:02:56,840
This is the last time the steam locomotive will run here,
you know.

30
00:02:57,280 --> 00:02:58,620
The line's being shut down, after all.

31
00:02:58,620 --> 00:02:59,440
This railway

32
00:02:59,940 --> 00:03:03,040
was one of the few railways
that still ran steam locomotives.

33
00:03:03,040 --> 00:03:04,440
It's really a shame.

34
00:03:08,300 --> 00:03:09,340
Ryo-chan

35
00:03:10,240 --> 00:03:13,540
Ryo-chan, over here, over here!

36
00:03:14,020 --> 00:03:15,000
Nori-chan

37
00:03:16,260 --> 00:03:18,760
I saved a seat for you, Ryo-chan.

38
00:03:18,760 --> 00:03:20,220
Thanks, Nori-chan.

39
00:03:20,800 --> 00:03:23,440
For my darling, it's the least I can do.

40
00:03:23,440 --> 00:03:25,160
"Darling"?

41
00:03:25,800 --> 00:03:29,020
Ryo-sama, after all we've been through,
how cruel of you!

42
00:03:29,440 --> 00:03:32,739
Don't get the wrong idea!
Nori-chan is just like you,

43
00:03:32,789 --> 00:03:34,200
a man with a P!

44
00:03:35,180 --> 00:03:36,644
Ryo-chan, who's she?

45
00:03:36,694 --> 00:03:39,420
This beauty... could she be your this?

46
00:03:40,220 --> 00:03:43,000
That'd be nice, but it's this way.

47
00:03:43,940 --> 00:03:45,296
Is that so?

48
00:03:45,346 --> 00:03:48,160
I think we'll get along well.
What's your name?

49
00:03:48,440 --> 00:03:51,820
I'm Asato Ai. Please call me Maria.

50
00:03:52,120 --> 00:03:55,760
Maria-chan I'm Nori-chan. Nice to meet you.

51
00:03:56,340 --> 00:03:57,420
Greetings can wait.

52
00:03:57,420 --> 00:03:59,800
Nori-chan, let me take your picture!

53
00:04:00,420 --> 00:04:02,100
Hey, everyone, well then -

54
00:04:02,100 --> 00:04:03,780
Excuse me.

55
00:04:04,280 --> 00:04:06,820
Ryo-chan,
help me once the shoot is over, okay?

56
00:04:07,440 --> 00:04:08,360
Leave it to me.

57
00:04:17,900 --> 00:04:19,660
Alright, the shoot's over!

58
00:04:19,660 --> 00:04:21,140
Business, business!

59
00:04:21,140 --> 00:04:24,720
This way for the famous Ōge okama bento!

60
00:04:25,760 --> 00:04:27,380
Come one, come all! Step right up!

61
00:04:27,520 --> 00:04:28,940
It's the okama!

62
00:04:29,800 --> 00:04:31,340
Hey, hey, my darlin'!

63
00:04:31,700 --> 00:04:32,060
Thank you very much!

64
00:04:33,640 --> 00:04:34,940
Here you are, sorry to keep you waiting!

65
00:04:35,140 --> 00:04:36,460
Yes, yes, here you go!

66
00:04:38,120 --> 00:04:38,480
Thank you!

67
00:04:40,940 --> 00:04:41,660
Thank you all!

68
00:04:48,020 --> 00:04:51,800
As always, the okama bento from
Nori-chan is hugely popular.

69
00:04:51,800 --> 00:04:53,940
Really, they've all sold out.

70
00:04:55,760 --> 00:05:00,460
We missed out What are you talking about? I've set aside yours and the others' portions,
Ryo-chan.

71
00:05:00,460 --> 00:05:04,020
As expected of Nori-chan.
Thanks for the meal!

72
00:05:06,460 --> 00:05:12,360
Delicious, right? This okama bento from Nori-chan,
made by her own hand, is the best ekiben in Japan.

73
00:05:13,060 --> 00:05:17,320
Thank you, Ryo-chan. But this is the last
time I'll be making it for you to eat.

74
00:05:19,660 --> 00:05:22,340
I'm getting older,
so I've been thinking about quitting.

75
00:05:22,920 --> 00:05:23,560
What did you say?

76
00:05:24,360 --> 00:05:28,040
I don't come here every year
just to see the steam locomotive.

77
00:05:28,680 --> 00:05:31,040
I come because I want to
eat this bento from Nori-chan.

78
00:05:31,460 --> 00:05:33,100
To think you'd go and quit that.

79
00:05:33,100 --> 00:05:36,200
I want to keep going too, you know.

80
00:05:37,420 --> 00:05:40,320
But if the line is being closed down,
there's nothing to be done about it.

81
00:05:40,320 --> 00:05:41,360
Nori-chan.

82
00:05:42,180 --> 00:05:43,800
Alright, I've got an idea.

83
00:05:44,180 --> 00:05:45,460
I won't let the line be closed.

84
00:05:46,300 --> 00:05:49,200
Just leave it to me, and trust me
like you're on a great big ship.

85
00:05:49,800 --> 00:05:50,740
Ryo-chan.

86
00:05:56,320 --> 00:05:59,900
Ryo-sama, is it really wise to
make such a reckless promise?

87
00:05:59,980 --> 00:06:01,140
Don't worry about it.

88
00:06:01,140 --> 00:06:05,400
I've got Nakagawa,
my walking cash box, after all.

89
00:06:05,400 --> 00:06:06,940
Ryo-sama, you really are something.

90
00:06:07,900 --> 00:06:10,580
But I'm a little jealous of Nori-chan.

91
00:06:10,580 --> 00:06:12,280
Hey, don't get the wrong idea.

92
00:06:12,280 --> 00:06:14,420
What I'm after is the taste of that ekiben,

93
00:06:14,420 --> 00:06:17,300
I just want to keep a
good memory with Nori-chan.

94
00:06:17,300 --> 00:06:18,240
Memories?

95
00:06:19,280 --> 00:06:21,580
That was decades ago.

96
00:06:22,340 --> 00:06:24,191
When I was still in elementary school,

97
00:06:24,241 --> 00:06:27,180
I had a fight with my father
and ran away from home.

98
00:06:28,200 --> 00:06:31,580
Though I ran away, I soon ran out of money.

99
00:06:32,460 --> 00:06:33,478
I was starving,

100
00:06:33,528 --> 00:06:36,580
and I sat on a bench at the station earlier,
lost and not knowing what to do.

101
00:06:40,740 --> 00:06:43,780
You must be hungry.
Here, have some if you like.

102
00:06:46,420 --> 00:06:47,880
But I don't have a single penny.

103
00:06:48,680 --> 00:06:51,360
They're leftovers,
so I don't need any money.

104
00:06:52,760 --> 00:06:53,120
Thank you.

105
00:06:58,500 --> 00:06:59,720
Nori-chan, you know,

106
00:06:59,720 --> 00:07:02,880
didn't ask me why I
ran away or even my name.

107
00:07:03,560 --> 00:07:05,120
She just smiled at me.

108
00:07:05,540 --> 00:07:08,660
On top of that, she even gave me
money for the train ticket home.

109
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:11,680
The taste of that bento,

110
00:07:11,680 --> 00:07:14,840
and Nori-chan's kindness,
I still remember them today.

111
00:07:16,240 --> 00:07:18,880
Nori-chan herself has
aged quite a bit, though.

112
00:07:19,260 --> 00:07:21,280
What a lovely story, Ryo-sama.

113
00:07:30,440 --> 00:07:32,820
What, you're quitting the police force?

114
00:07:33,320 --> 00:07:39,780
Actually, I've been roped into a huge project that
will decide the fate of every Nakagawa Group company.

115
00:07:39,780 --> 00:07:42,380
A huge project? What is it?

116
00:07:42,760 --> 00:07:50,340
It's an outrageous plan to build a road across the Pacific,
linking Japan and America, by the year 2033.

117
00:07:51,080 --> 00:07:52,320
That's 35 years from now

118
00:07:52,740 --> 00:07:56,720
Ryo-sama, if Mr. Nakagawa is gone,
then Nori-chan...

119
00:07:57,900 --> 00:07:58,740
Aaaaah!

120
00:07:58,740 --> 00:07:59,220
Aaaaah!

121
00:07:59,620 --> 00:08:03,780
Don't be ridiculous! Police work is your main job.
Just turn that nonsense down!

122
00:08:03,780 --> 00:08:08,120
Of course I refused!
But my father won't let me.

123
00:08:08,120 --> 00:08:11,340
You joined the police because you love being a cop,
didn't you?

124
00:08:11,340 --> 00:08:15,360
Is it really okay to quit so easily
just because your dad gave you orders?

125
00:08:15,360 --> 00:08:16,940
Senpai.

126
00:08:16,940 --> 00:08:18,600
I'm saddened.

127
00:08:18,600 --> 00:08:23,860
I believed Nakagawa was a man
born to become a police officer.

128
00:08:24,600 --> 00:08:27,300
Senpai, going this far for me...

129
00:08:27,300 --> 00:08:28,780
Just one more push.

130
00:08:28,780 --> 00:08:32,280
When you think of Ryo-chan and Kei-chan,
the duo from Kōen-mae,

131
00:08:32,280 --> 00:08:36,780
I thought you two would make a
better duo than Aozora Kyūji and Kōji.

132
00:08:36,780 --> 00:08:38,860
Are you two a manzai comedy act or what?

133
00:08:38,860 --> 00:08:42,400
Chief, are you saying Nakagawa can quit?

134
00:08:42,400 --> 00:08:44,300
W-well, that's not what I'm saying.

135
00:08:44,300 --> 00:08:46,120
Then stop him, please.

136
00:08:47,580 --> 00:08:50,320
Nakagawa, why don't you try
talking it over with your father?

137
00:08:50,320 --> 00:08:52,100
I hadn't thought of that.

138
00:08:52,780 --> 00:08:54,500
Alright, I'll talk him into it.

139
00:08:54,900 --> 00:08:55,860
S-senpai...

140
00:08:57,080 --> 00:09:00,940
Speaking of which,
I've never once seen Nakagawa's father.

141
00:09:01,480 --> 00:09:03,280
I've never met him either.

142
00:09:03,280 --> 00:09:04,320
Me neither.

143
00:09:04,320 --> 00:09:08,060
Actually, I've only met him
about three times since I was born.

144
00:09:08,420 --> 00:09:10,120
I can't even remember his face.

145
00:09:11,400 --> 00:09:12,120
What?!

146
00:09:12,700 --> 00:09:14,340
What kind of father is he?

147
00:09:14,340 --> 00:09:16,020
He's a super businessman.

148
00:09:16,940 --> 00:09:18,940
Apparently he only sleeps
five minutes every three days.

149
00:09:19,480 --> 00:09:23,620
He's still a company man who works 72 hours straight,
you know.

150
00:09:23,620 --> 00:09:26,560
Don't you have any photos
of your family or something?

151
00:09:27,120 --> 00:09:28,400
Well, I do have some.

152
00:09:30,700 --> 00:09:33,340
This is the only photo with my father in it.

153
00:09:33,340 --> 00:09:36,040
Your father's like Nesco's Nessie, isn't he?

154
00:09:36,820 --> 00:09:39,940
His name is officially
given as Ryuichiro Nakagawa,

155
00:09:40,360 --> 00:09:42,380
but we can't reach him from our end.

156
00:09:42,380 --> 00:09:45,100
After all,
he's always running around the world.

157
00:09:46,940 --> 00:09:53,260
Go ahead and try, but I don't think it'll work.
You want to quit being a cop? Understood.

158
00:10:00,320 --> 00:10:07,240
This is Keiichi Nakagawa. I'd like to see the president,
but I need to make an appointment.

159
00:10:07,780 --> 00:10:09,400
I can't believe he's
your own flesh and blood.

160
00:10:09,400 --> 00:10:10,300
Hello.

161
00:10:11,180 --> 00:10:17,300
They said I can meet him for three minutes,
starting at 11 p.m. on December 31st, eleven years from now.

162
00:10:17,300 --> 00:10:20,280
What? Don't give me that nonsense.

163
00:10:20,280 --> 00:10:21,500
Give me that.

164
00:10:21,960 --> 00:10:25,000
Hey, your own son is
coming to see you, so...

165
00:10:25,780 --> 00:10:26,180
Yeah.

166
00:10:27,400 --> 00:10:28,900
Shit, he hung up.

167
00:10:29,620 --> 00:10:32,180
Nakagawa, in that case,
we're going to see him in person.

168
00:10:33,520 --> 00:10:34,840
Wait, senpai.

169
00:10:38,300 --> 00:10:40,220
His father's schedule

170
00:10:40,900 --> 00:10:42,620
He's really a cold-blooded bastard,
isn't he?

171
00:10:43,240 --> 00:10:45,160
He won't stay in one place for even five minutes,
will he?

172
00:10:45,780 --> 00:10:48,740
Lucky for us, he's back in Japan
for the first time in ten years.

173
00:10:49,240 --> 00:10:51,860
He's scheduled to stay for
another eight hours and 25 minutes.

174
00:10:51,860 --> 00:10:54,680
His next visit won't be until eleven years from now,
you know.

175
00:10:55,080 --> 00:10:57,140
He's a father like Halley's Comet, isn't he?

176
00:10:57,500 --> 00:10:58,140
There he is.

177
00:10:59,060 --> 00:10:59,780
That's it.

178
00:11:01,260 --> 00:11:02,380
What a freak.

179
00:11:02,380 --> 00:11:04,360
Look at all those
helicopters attached to it!

180
00:11:18,940 --> 00:11:20,020
I see. I see.

181
00:11:20,710 --> 00:11:22,160
Nothing unusual.

182
00:11:24,640 --> 00:11:25,180
Heh.

183
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:38,760
The president will arrive in 30 seconds.

184
00:11:38,760 --> 00:11:41,180
Please, just stamp this financial statement.

185
00:11:41,180 --> 00:11:43,520
Alright, I'll give you just 15 seconds.

186
00:11:47,620 --> 00:11:48,740
Then, here, sign this.

187
00:11:49,960 --> 00:11:50,920
Wow.

188
00:11:51,900 --> 00:11:52,380
Thank you very much.

189
00:11:54,480 --> 00:11:57,060
President, stamp these documents too.

190
00:11:57,060 --> 00:12:01,180
The answer is no. Time's up.

191
00:12:01,180 --> 00:12:02,460
I'm terribly sorry.

192
00:12:03,260 --> 00:12:05,220
The remaining 15 seconds are drink time.

193
00:12:12,380 --> 00:12:14,060
Which one would you prefer?

194
00:12:14,760 --> 00:12:16,380
Just a little drowsy

195
00:12:16,880 --> 00:12:19,580
Then, the Suppon Mamushi
Ultra Super Drink, please.

196
00:12:22,460 --> 00:12:23,100
Here you go.

197
00:12:29,920 --> 00:12:31,140
Here it comes, here it comes, here it comes!

198
00:12:57,400 --> 00:12:58,540
Getting off

199
00:12:58,540 --> 00:13:00,580
We're getting off the express too

200
00:13:02,640 --> 00:13:04,700
Impossible, we're completely blocked in.

201
00:13:09,620 --> 00:13:11,440
You're five seconds late.

202
00:13:11,440 --> 00:13:14,120
The deal's off. We're going home.

203
00:13:16,020 --> 00:13:17,000
President Nakagawa

204
00:13:17,500 --> 00:13:19,300
I'm sorry for the delay.

205
00:13:19,300 --> 00:13:21,160
There was an accident jam on the expressway.

206
00:13:22,240 --> 00:13:26,000
No excuses. Let's pretend this
conversation never happened.

207
00:13:26,760 --> 00:13:29,060
A business opportunity only comes once.

208
00:13:29,060 --> 00:13:29,580
No way.

209
00:13:30,920 --> 00:13:32,460
President, sorry to keep you waiting!

210
00:13:37,160 --> 00:13:39,320
We'd barely landed before we took off again.

211
00:13:39,560 --> 00:13:42,840
Don't be impressed.
Was that Dad who just boarded?

212
00:13:43,540 --> 00:13:46,620
Maybe. I honestly can't remember very well.

213
00:13:49,120 --> 00:13:51,080
President Adam has just arrived.

214
00:13:51,920 --> 00:13:54,160
Understood. I'll be there in three minutes.

215
00:14:05,940 --> 00:14:07,220
Welcome back.

216
00:14:09,500 --> 00:14:12,400
President Adam is waiting for you
in the VIP room on the 35th floor.

217
00:14:12,400 --> 00:14:13,440
Understood.

218
00:14:14,840 --> 00:14:16,160
We've arrived right on time.

219
00:14:16,160 --> 00:14:18,040
This is President Nakagawa.

220
00:14:18,040 --> 00:14:20,100
Mr. Nakagawa!

221
00:14:20,100 --> 00:14:23,000
I believe the contract terms
were explained to you in advance.

222
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:25,760
We don't have much time,
so I'd like your answer right away.

223
00:14:25,760 --> 00:14:28,740
Blah blah blah blah blah blah blah.

224
00:14:28,740 --> 00:14:29,820
Blah blah blah blah blah.

225
00:14:30,820 --> 00:14:32,960
He says it's an honor to meet you,
Mr. Nakagawa.

226
00:14:32,960 --> 00:14:34,540
Let's make this an opportunity,
by all means.

227
00:14:35,240 --> 00:14:36,740
I didn't hear anything about this!

228
00:14:36,740 --> 00:14:38,620
Yes or no, which is it?

229
00:14:38,620 --> 00:14:39,880
Yes.

230
00:14:39,880 --> 00:14:40,780
Okay.

231
00:14:42,520 --> 00:14:44,040
Right on schedule. Wonderful.

232
00:14:44,840 --> 00:14:45,940
It's written in the contract.

233
00:14:45,940 --> 00:14:47,180
Leave the rest to you.

234
00:14:47,180 --> 00:14:47,620
Yes.

235
00:14:52,280 --> 00:14:53,580
The helicopter has come to pick you up.

236
00:14:55,340 --> 00:14:56,160
Let's go.

237
00:14:57,880 --> 00:14:59,740
Head straight to the next site.

238
00:15:01,720 --> 00:15:02,820
Thank you for your hard work.

239
00:15:03,340 --> 00:15:05,020
Mm, I'm a little tired.

240
00:15:07,280 --> 00:15:09,880
I'm going to sleep for one minute.
Don't wake me, no matter what.

241
00:15:09,880 --> 00:15:10,520
Yes.

242
00:15:21,360 --> 00:15:22,760
We finally caught up!

243
00:15:23,520 --> 00:15:25,180
Now there are no bodyguards!

244
00:15:25,180 --> 00:15:26,580
Pull the helicopter alongside.

245
00:15:26,580 --> 00:15:26,900
Yes.

246
00:15:29,820 --> 00:15:32,260
Hey, Nakagawa's father, can you hear me?

247
00:15:38,200 --> 00:15:39,720
But there are still five seconds left!

248
00:15:40,280 --> 00:15:41,860
I told you not to wake him up,
after all that!

249
00:15:42,280 --> 00:15:43,320
I'm terribly sorry.

250
00:15:43,320 --> 00:15:45,700
The helicopter came approaching
without an appointment, so...

251
00:15:49,320 --> 00:15:51,560
Hey, Nakagawa's father, can you hear me?

252
00:15:52,140 --> 00:15:52,760
How dirty!

253
00:15:52,760 --> 00:15:54,180
A big shot has come to see you!

254
00:15:54,180 --> 00:15:55,540
Nakagawa, you say something too!

255
00:15:55,540 --> 00:15:56,220
Father.

256
00:15:57,020 --> 00:15:58,520
Let us through.

257
00:15:59,220 --> 00:16:00,100
What a guy!

258
00:16:00,100 --> 00:16:02,360
If it comes to this, I'll force a meeting!

259
00:16:03,540 --> 00:16:05,040
Hey, park on the helipad!

260
00:16:05,040 --> 00:16:05,500
Yes.

261
00:16:09,840 --> 00:16:12,360
Just wait, I'm coming right now.

262
00:16:19,240 --> 00:16:21,900
I'm busy, you know.

263
00:16:24,060 --> 00:16:25,120
Not so fast, you don't get away.

264
00:16:26,900 --> 00:16:27,820
He jumped out!

265
00:16:27,920 --> 00:16:28,360
That's reckless!

266
00:16:29,200 --> 00:16:30,960
Yes! Buy up all those shares!

267
00:16:31,140 --> 00:16:32,120
Noooooo!

268
00:16:32,320 --> 00:16:33,420
What! Got you!

269
00:16:34,280 --> 00:16:35,980
Hey, that's rude! I'm on the phone!

270
00:16:36,220 --> 00:16:37,200
Listen to me!

271
00:16:38,520 --> 00:16:40,140
Then I'll give you ten seconds!

272
00:16:40,420 --> 00:16:43,040
Yes! Don't put my son Keichi on the project!

273
00:16:43,320 --> 00:16:44,700
Cancel it right now!

274
00:16:45,380 --> 00:16:46,380
The answer is no!

275
00:16:47,460 --> 00:16:48,360
Ten seconds are up!

276
00:16:49,740 --> 00:16:51,360
Noooooo!

277
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:06,740
Sorry to keep you waiting, sir.

278
00:17:07,760 --> 00:17:09,380
So you had a car ready?

279
00:17:21,120 --> 00:17:22,920
Who is it at a busy time like this?

280
00:17:25,580 --> 00:17:26,440
Ryo-chan?

281
00:17:27,120 --> 00:17:29,360
What is it? Nori-chan? What's wrong?

282
00:17:29,720 --> 00:17:30,939
I've been thinking,

283
00:17:30,989 --> 00:17:35,080
and I can't keep causing you trouble,
Ryo-chan.

284
00:17:36,600 --> 00:17:40,320
So I've decided to give up
completely and go back to Hokkaido.

285
00:17:40,660 --> 00:17:42,360
What? Where are you right now?

286
00:17:42,760 --> 00:17:43,680
At the airport.

287
00:17:43,880 --> 00:17:46,390
Idiot! If Nori-chan goes home,

288
00:17:46,440 --> 00:17:48,520
I'm quitting the police force!

289
00:17:48,860 --> 00:17:52,020
I'll stake my life on it.
We are not losing, period!

290
00:17:52,120 --> 00:17:53,780
Cancel the plane and wait!

291
00:17:54,240 --> 00:17:54,700
Got it?

292
00:17:59,320 --> 00:17:59,660
Hey.

293
00:18:00,480 --> 00:18:01,820
I'm borrowing a bicycle.

294
00:18:01,820 --> 00:18:03,660
Come on, get off, get off.

295
00:18:11,480 --> 00:18:12,160
President.

296
00:18:12,160 --> 00:18:13,920
A call from the Brazil branch office...

297
00:18:14,360 --> 00:18:15,280
As scheduled.

298
00:18:23,260 --> 00:18:24,480
How's it going? On schedule?

299
00:18:27,600 --> 00:18:28,840
I see... I don't quite follow.

300
00:18:28,840 --> 00:18:31,220
I'll be there in three minutes.

301
00:18:37,260 --> 00:18:38,100
You!

302
00:18:38,100 --> 00:18:39,380
We caught up!

303
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:43,200
Hey! I'm calling the police!

304
00:18:43,200 --> 00:18:43,860
Hey, Nyu.

305
00:18:43,860 --> 00:18:45,120
I am the police!

306
00:18:46,100 --> 00:18:47,220
The police!

307
00:18:48,860 --> 00:18:51,180
I know you won't listen to me!

308
00:18:51,980 --> 00:18:52,820
Fine.

309
00:18:52,820 --> 00:18:54,260
I'll give you 15 seconds.

310
00:18:54,880 --> 00:18:58,360
Alright! Your son doesn't want
to take part in the project!

311
00:18:58,680 --> 00:19:00,400
Remove Nakagawa from the project!

312
00:19:01,020 --> 00:19:02,220
The answer is NO!

313
00:19:03,320 --> 00:19:05,720
The project is already underway!

314
00:19:06,240 --> 00:19:07,360
Damn it! Wait!

315
00:19:15,100 --> 00:19:16,740
It's Nakagawa's helicopter! Is it good?

316
00:19:20,180 --> 00:19:21,780
Hey! You can't run away anymore!

317
00:19:22,320 --> 00:19:22,980
Father!

318
00:19:24,080 --> 00:19:26,980
His son's here too!
Make sure you listen to him properly!

319
00:19:31,440 --> 00:19:33,920
It's nothing.
It's just the signal for mealtime.

320
00:19:34,820 --> 00:19:37,980
I'll make an exception and give you five minutes.
Let's hear what you have to say.

321
00:19:38,280 --> 00:19:39,080
Don't startle me!

322
00:19:40,260 --> 00:19:43,780
I never expected a big-shot president
like you to eat at a place like this.

323
00:19:44,000 --> 00:19:47,720
Speed is the most important thing. Whenever I come to Japan,
I always eat standing soba.

324
00:19:48,140 --> 00:19:49,580
You could just use a cell phone.

325
00:19:49,580 --> 00:19:51,240
Why use such a radio?

326
00:19:52,240 --> 00:19:53,660
Because I don't want to be wiretapped.

327
00:19:53,660 --> 00:19:56,340
We change the frequency
every time to keep in contact.

328
00:19:57,880 --> 00:19:59,700
By the way, K-12, I...

329
00:20:01,600 --> 00:20:02,240
Excuse me.

330
00:20:02,240 --> 00:20:03,780
Hey, are you running away?

331
00:20:04,340 --> 00:20:06,560
Reception is bad inside here.

332
00:20:10,060 --> 00:20:12,560
Hotline, this is White Rock, over.

333
00:20:13,020 --> 00:20:14,920
You sound like a radio operator.

334
00:20:14,920 --> 00:20:17,660
My father has always hated
leaving things to others,

335
00:20:17,660 --> 00:20:19,880
so he reportedly did everything himself.

336
00:20:19,880 --> 00:20:22,380
So that's why he lives such
a relentlessly busy life.

337
00:20:22,380 --> 00:20:23,300
Keiichi.

338
00:20:23,300 --> 00:20:24,260
Yes.

339
00:20:24,700 --> 00:20:28,080
The Pacific crossing road
project has been postponed.

340
00:20:29,840 --> 00:20:33,400
Apparently it will start in 2098,
a hundred years from now.

341
00:20:33,860 --> 00:20:36,120
They just decided to review it.

342
00:20:36,120 --> 00:20:37,960
R-really?

343
00:20:37,960 --> 00:20:43,180
Phew, good thing you don't have to quit being a cop!
Thank you, senior.

344
00:20:44,820 --> 00:20:46,940
Heiichi yes!

345
00:20:48,720 --> 00:20:55,640
I haven't seen you in twenty years, but you've grown up well.
Otoko-san suddenly seems like a proper father!

346
00:20:57,580 --> 00:20:59,400
Excuse me, it's drink time!

347
00:21:09,240 --> 00:21:11,720
Here it comes! Here it comes! Here it comes!

348
00:21:17,280 --> 00:21:20,580
I really feel like I could
work for 72 hours straight.

349
00:21:21,520 --> 00:21:24,080
Sorry for causing such a fuss this time,
Keiichi.

350
00:21:24,500 --> 00:21:27,800
I'd love to meet your mother
and the others properly sometime.

351
00:21:29,400 --> 00:21:31,840
I secretly see Mom every year.

352
00:21:31,840 --> 00:21:33,240
Really?

353
00:21:33,640 --> 00:21:36,100
Listen, this is a secret from everyone.

354
00:21:36,580 --> 00:21:38,220
Y-yes, understood.

355
00:21:39,420 --> 00:21:44,520
Still, you're lucky to have a
senior who'd risk his life for you.

356
00:21:44,520 --> 00:21:45,160
Yes.

357
00:21:45,800 --> 00:21:48,700
Please keep looking after Keiichi,
Mr. Ryotsu.

358
00:21:48,700 --> 00:21:50,180
Yes, thank you.

359
00:21:52,280 --> 00:21:52,960
It's time.

360
00:22:00,080 --> 00:22:01,240
Well then, farewell.

361
00:22:01,240 --> 00:22:03,380
The next time I come will be in 2009.

362
00:22:03,380 --> 00:22:04,800
Stay well until then.

363
00:22:04,800 --> 00:22:06,440
You too, Dad, stay well.

364
00:22:06,440 --> 00:22:08,660
Farewell.

365
00:22:13,940 --> 00:22:16,120
So you won't have to quit after all.

366
00:22:16,120 --> 00:22:17,780
I'm so glad, Kei-chan.

367
00:22:17,780 --> 00:22:19,960
This is all thanks to you, senpai.

368
00:22:19,960 --> 00:22:21,640
No, I didn't really do anything.

369
00:22:23,120 --> 00:22:24,340
By the way, Nakagawa.

370
00:22:24,340 --> 00:22:26,860
There's something I'd like to ask of you.

371
00:22:27,340 --> 00:22:28,760
If it's something I can do...

372
00:22:29,400 --> 00:22:30,860
Well, go ahead and tell me. Really?

373
00:22:31,520 --> 00:22:32,780
Aaaaaah!

374
00:22:37,840 --> 00:22:42,100
Sure, I can do it,
even if it breaks my bones, nagaa!

375
00:22:42,960 --> 00:22:52,000
Really, thank you so much! Didn't I tell you to leave it to me?
Nice to meet you, I'm Nakagawa. Thank you for everything this time.

376
00:22:52,800 --> 00:22:57,120
Please keep supporting our famous Toge no Okama bento,
won't you?

377
00:22:57,120 --> 00:22:59,120
Yes, thank you very much.

378
00:23:00,420 --> 00:23:02,800
Nakagawa Railway's first
thank-you has arrived!

379
00:23:09,780 --> 00:23:11,720
Step right up, step right up!

380
00:23:11,720 --> 00:23:15,640
How about our famous Toge no Okama bento?

381
00:23:15,640 --> 00:23:17,580
Come on, buy, buy!

382
00:23:18,860 --> 00:23:19,260
Thank you very much.

383
00:23:20,100 --> 00:23:20,480
Thank you very much.

384
00:23:21,580 --> 00:23:22,420
Here you go.

385
00:23:23,720 --> 00:23:25,320
Sorry to keep you waiting.

386
00:23:25,320 --> 00:23:27,620
Welcome!

387
00:23:28,840 --> 00:23:30,580
Looking forward to working
with you from now on.

388
00:23:30,580 --> 00:23:34,240
Knowing Ryo-chan,
I figured something was up,

389
00:23:34,240 --> 00:23:37,280
but I never expected you'd
have us buy a railway company.

390
00:23:37,280 --> 00:23:38,880
Sounds just like you, senpai.

391
00:23:39,340 --> 00:23:41,780
Going to all this trouble
for a friend's ekiben.

392
00:23:42,340 --> 00:23:43,480
But are you going to be okay?

393
00:23:43,480 --> 00:23:46,760
Buying a railway that
loses 3 billion a year?

394
00:23:47,120 --> 00:23:51,180
As long as I can keep being a cop,
3 billion is no big deal.

395
00:23:51,800 --> 00:23:52,800
Hey, Nakagawa!

396
00:23:53,160 --> 00:23:53,520
Yes?

397
00:23:53,880 --> 00:23:55,520
What are you gawking at?

398
00:23:55,520 --> 00:23:57,040
Help out, help out!

399
00:23:57,040 --> 00:23:57,900
R-right!

400
00:24:04,520 --> 00:24:06,640
It's you again, Professor Esaki.

401
00:24:06,640 --> 00:24:08,900
Sanson, café au lait, Citroën...

402
00:24:08,900 --> 00:24:11,080
When did you get so
carried away with France?

403
00:24:11,640 --> 00:24:14,040
I've told you,
we don't need your inventions anymore.

404
00:24:14,460 --> 00:24:15,580
Don't try to change the subject!

405
00:24:17,780 --> 00:24:21,600
Next time: a delusional, outrageous new invention.
See you then!

406
00:24:46,820 --> 00:24:49,860
Set in stone, a flash of inspiration

407
00:24:49,860 --> 00:24:52,740
bouncing along, all tied together

408
00:24:52,740 --> 00:24:55,700
acting, soaring onward

409
00:24:56,360 --> 00:25:00,400
more than anything, incredible power

410
00:25:00,400 --> 00:25:06,400
gather everyone here

411
00:25:07,200 --> 00:25:12,720
like a dream, the final energy

412
00:25:13,980 --> 00:25:20,040
gaze at tomorrow, believe in yesterday,
paint the sky, and stand on the ground

413
00:25:20,040 --> 00:25:23,820
the star of Kameari spun
round and drew a circle

414
00:25:26,080 --> 00:25:27,480
That should be fine, right?

415
00:25:27,480 --> 00:25:28,940
Like hell it is.

416
00:25:42,720 --> 00:25:43,800
Thank you for watching.

